transcriptId":"CROX_Q3_2026","companyId":7,"title":"Crocs FY2026 Q3 Earnings Call","type":"transcript","quarter":"Q3","fiscalYear":"FY2026","sourceUrl":"https://investors.crocs.com/news-and-events/press-releases/press-release-details/2026/Crocs-Inc--Reports-Strong-Third-Quarter-2026-Results-Raises-Full-Year-2026-Outlook/default.aspx","summary":"Crocs Q3 2026 revenue increased 5% to more than $1 billion, with Crocs Brand up 4% and HEYDUDE up 6%. Management raised full-year revenue and EPS guidance, highlighted HEYDUDE's return to growth, and quantified the North America DTC-to-wholesale business-model shift while maintaining disciplined promotion and inventory management.","ceoRemarks":"","cfoRemarks":"","highlights":[],"revenueDrivers":"International Crocs DTC growth, HEYDUDE wholesale recovery, product diversification, easier wholesale comparisons, and social-commerce expansion.","marginDrivers":"Lower tariffs, supply-chain cost savings, higher ASPs and channel mix, partially offset by planned product-mix headwinds.","guidance":"FY2026 enterprise revenue growth approximately 3%; Crocs Brand approximately 4%; HEYDUDE approximately flat; Q4 enterprise growth 7%-9%; adjusted EPS $14.45-$14.65.","risks":"K-shaped consumer pressure, cautious wholesale ordering, elevated input-cost inflation, competitive holiday promotions, and temporary DTC reporting headwinds from the business-model shift.","publishedAt":"2026-10-29T20:30:00+08:00","paragraphCount":218},{"id":2,"transcriptId":"NKE_FY2027_Q1","companyId":1,"title":"Nike FY2027 Q1 Earnings Call","type":"transcript","quarter":"Q1","fiscalYear":"FY2027","sourceUrl":"https://investors.nike.com/investors/news-events-and-reports/investor-news/investor-news-details/2026/NIKE-Inc--Reports-Fiscal-2027-First-Quarter-Results/default.aspx","summary":"Nike FY2027 Q1 revenue was $11.2 billion, down 4% reported and 5% currency neutral. Gross margin improved to 42.8% and performance categories grew, while Sportswear, Jordan Brand, and Greater China remained under pressure. Pace savings are expected to scale mainly in FY2029-FY2030.","ceoRemarks":"","cfoRemarks":"","highlights":["Performance portfolio grew high single digits","Greater China revenue declined 26%","Gross margin improved 60 basis points to 42.8%","Pace savings are expected to scale in FY2029-FY2030","FY2027 revenue is expected to decline high single digits"],"revenueDrivers":"Performance running, football, training, basketball, tennis and golf growth offset pressure in Sportswear, Jordan Brand and Greater China.","marginDrivers":"Supply-chain cost actions and FX helped gross margin, while discounts, channel mix, fixed-cost deleverage and reset actions remain pressures.","guidance":"FY2027 revenue expected to decline high single digits; adjusted EPS expected at $1.15-$1.35 excluding approximately $0.15 of Pace impact.","risks":"Greater China reset duration, Sportswear and Jordan repositioning, promotional comparisons, fixed-cost deleverage, and Pace execution.","publishedAt":"2026-10-01T21:00:00.000Z","paragraphCount":33},{"id":3,"transcriptId":"LULU_Q2_2026","companyId":2,"title":"Lululemon FY2026 Q2 Earnings Call","type":"transcript","quarter":"Q2","fiscalYear":"FY2026","sourceUrl":"https://corporate.lululemon.com/newsroom/press-releases/2026/09-03-2026-210528733","summary":"Lululemon FY2026 第二季度收入下降 4% 至 24 亿美元，北美下降 8%；中国大陆按报告口径增长 4%，按固定汇率计算下降 2%。管理层下调全年指引，加快畅销产品追单和品牌投入，并在保护产品与品牌能力的同时深入审视成本基础。","ceoRemarks":"","cfoRemarks":"","highlights":["第二季度收入下降 4%","北美收入下降 8%","中国大陆按报告口径增长 4%","IEEPA 关税退款增厚营业利润率","全年收入指引下调"],"revenueDrivers":"客流压力、新品上市反响不稳定、中国品牌情绪、国际市场趋势，以及追单和社区活动的推进速度。","marginDrivers":"关税退款、基础关税成本、降价、固定成本去杠杆、渠道及品类结构，以及激励薪酬应计费用冲回。","guidance":"FY2026 收入预计为 103.5 亿至 105 亿美元，同比下降 5% 至 7%；毛利率下降约 80 个基点；摊薄每股收益为 9.48 至 9.73 美元。","risks":"持续客流压力、产品市场反响不确定、中国品牌情绪、季节性清货、固定成本去杠杆和关税退款不确定性。","publishedAt":"2026-09-03T20:30:00.000Z","paragraphCount":131},{"id":4,"transcriptId":"AS_Q2_2026","companyId":4,"title":"Amer Sports Q2 2026 Earnings Call","type":"transcript","quarter":"Q2","fiscalYear":"FY2026","sourceUrl":"https://www.marketbeat.com/earnings/reports/2026-8-18-amer-sports-inc-stock/","summary":"Amer Sports Q2 2026 revenue grew 32% reported and 30% ex-currency, led by DTC, Arc’teryx, Salomon and Wilson Tennis 360. Adjusted gross margin rose to 65.8%, with a one-time net tariff refund contributing 390 basis points; underlying gross margin expansion exceeded 300 basis points. Management raised full-year revenue, margin and EPS guidance while continuing to invest in brand, retail and digital capabilities.","ceoRemarks":"","cfoRemarks":"","highlights":[],"revenueDrivers":"","marginDrivers":"","guidance":"","risks":"","publishedAt":"2026-08-18T20:00:00+08:00","paragraphCount":38},{"id":5,"transcriptId":"ONON_Q2_2026","companyId":6,"title":"On Holding 2026 Q2 Earnings Call","type":"transcript","quarter":"Q2","fiscalYear":"FY2026","sourceUrl":"https://files.quartr.com/reports/f256250f73a2f366f5a09a58ece0354b-2026-08-11-09-59-20.pdf?ref=TWFya2V0QmVhdCBNZWRpYSBMTEM=","summary":"On Holding 2026 年第二季度收入按固定汇率增长 21.6%，直营渠道增长 34.3%，批发渠道管理层主动收紧向渠道发货以保护全价体系和后续新品承接。公司将全年固定汇率收入增长指引维持在低 20% 区间，并将全年毛利率指引上调至至少 65%。","ceoRemarks":"","cfoRemarks":"","highlights":["直营渠道固定汇率增长 34.3%","批发渠道主动管理发货节奏","毛利率指引上调至至少 65%","新增客群与多品类扩张继续推进","价格区间向更高层级延展"],"revenueDrivers":"直营渠道增长、欧洲中东及非洲地区表现、运动生活方式和服装品类扩张，以及技术新品带来的需求","marginDrivers":"直营渠道占比提升、全价销售执行、产品与渠道结构，以及批发渠道库存质量管理","guidance":"全年固定汇率收入增长低 20% 区间，绝对收入约 34.7 亿至 35.6 亿瑞士法郎，全年毛利率至少 65.0%，调整后 EBITDA 利润率 19.5% 至 20.0%","risks":"美国多品牌批发市场的促销压力、日常跑步产品售罄偏弱、批发发货节奏和关税退款确认时点","publishedAt":"2026-08-11T20:00:00+08:00","paragraphCount":131},{"id":6,"transcriptId":"ALPA4_Q2_2026","companyId":8,"title":"Alpargatas 2026 Q2 Earnings Call","type":"transcript","quarter":"Q2","fiscalYear":"2026","sourceUrl":"https://www.rad.cvm.gov.br/ENETCONSULTA/frmDownloadDocumento.aspx?CodigoInstituicao=1&Tela=99&descTipo=IPE&numProtocolo=1553688&numSequencia=1078394&numVersao=1","summary":"Alpargatas Q2 2026 net sales reached R$1.226 billion, up 11.3%, with adjusted EBITDA of R$286 million and a 23.3% margin. Brazil sell-out grew 13%, Europe volume grew 21%, and the U.S. distributor model improved cost efficiency. Rothy's reported US$61.2 million revenue and a 67% gross margin including a tariff refund.","ceoRemarks":"","cfoRemarks":"","highlights":["Global volume increased 9%","Brazil sell-out increased 13%","Europe volume increased 21%","Adjusted EBITDA margin reached 23.3%","Rothy's gross margin included a tariff-refund benefit"],"revenueDrivers":"Brazil volume, premium product mix, Europe recovery, and broader U.S. distribution supported revenue; Rothy's online sales remained soft.","marginDrivers":"Manufacturing and logistics efficiency, regional mix, U.S. fixed-cost removal, and scale recovery supported margins; Rothy's reported gross margin included a one-off tariff refund.","guidance":"Management did not provide formal guidance and emphasized calibrated growth, price-elasticity-based decisions, and order visibility in the fourth quarter.","risks":"Raw-material volatility, foreign exchange, execution capacity, international service levels, estimated sell-out data, and Rothy's online-sales gap.","publishedAt":"2026-08-07T12:00:00.000Z","paragraphCount":162},{"id":7,"transcriptId":"CROX_Q2_2026","companyId":7,"title":"Crocs FY2026 Q2 Earnings Call","type":"transcript","quarter":"Q2","fiscalYear":"FY2026","sourceUrl":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1334036/000133403626000050/croxq22026-pressrelease.htm","summary":"Crocs 第二季度收入约 12 亿美元，同比增长 2%；Crocs 品牌首次单季超过 10 亿美元，HEYDUDE 收入下降 6% 但好于预期。直营增长、促销减少和国际市场改善支撑收入，关税使调整后毛利率下降 170 个基点。公司上调全年收入和每股收益指引，并披露一项影响渠道收入确认但不改变终端销量的业务模式调整。","ceoRemarks":"","cfoRemarks":"","highlights":["Crocs brand exceeded $1 billion","Both brands delivered DTC growth","International Crocs revenue grew 7%","HEYDUDE trajectory improved","Full-year revenue and EPS guidance increased"],"revenueDrivers":"International growth, sandals and clog diversification, digital marketplaces, new stores, and improving HEYDUDE direct-to-consumer demand.","marginDrivers":"Tariffs, product and channel mix, cost savings, international price increases, and targeted direct-to-consumer investment.","guidance":"FY2026 enterprise revenue growth of 1%-2%, Crocs brand growth of 2%-3%, HEYDUDE down 2%-4%, and adjusted diluted EPS of $13.70-$14.00.","risks":"North America wholesale declines, revenue-recognition comparability, tariff pressure, HEYDUDE's fourth-quarter acceleration, and channel inventory execution.","publishedAt":"2026-07-30T20:30:00.000Z","paragraphCount":117},{"id":8,"transcriptId":"DECK_Q1_2027","companyId":3,"title":"Deckers FY2027 Q1 Earnings Call","type":"transcript","quarter":"Q1","fiscalYear":"FY2027","sourceUrl":"https://ir.deckers.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/661/deckers-brands-reports-first-quarter-fiscal-year-2027-financial-results","summary":"Deckers 第一季度收入 10.2 亿美元，同比增长 5.7%；HOKA 增长 8%，UGG 增长 5%，直营增长继续快于批发。毛利率升至 56.4%，全价销售、渠道结构和清仓管理抵消了部分关税影响。公司维持全年收入区间，并把关税假设从 10% 上调至 12.5%。","ceoRemarks":"","cfoRemarks":"","highlights":["DTC growth led the quarter","Full-price demand remained healthy","Inventory declined 5%","Gross-margin outlook increased","Tariff assumption raised to 12.5%"],"revenueDrivers":"HOKA and UGG full-price demand, international DTC growth, product newness, and later international wholesale shipment timing.","marginDrivers":"Favorable channel and product mix, full-price selling, better closeout management, foreign exchange, and tariff pressure.","guidance":"FY2027 revenue of $5.86-$5.91 billion, gross margin slightly above 56.5%, operating margin slightly above 21.5%, and diluted EPS of $7.35-$7.50.","risks":"Higher tariffs, freight costs, second-half wholesale shipment timing, product transitions, and the durability of full-price demand.","publishedAt":"2026-07-23T20:30:00.000Z","paragraphCount":91},{"id":9,"transcriptId":"NKE_FY2026_Q4","companyId":1,"title":"Nike FY2026